    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. Here's a summary of the change I implemented.\n\n## What was required\nThe `POST /api/owners` request may include an optional `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR), and owners expose a derived `salutation` = `title + ' ' + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\n## Changes made\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** (the source of the generated DTOs):\n   - Added an optional `title` property (enum `MR/MRS/MS/DR`) to the `OwnerFields` schema, so it's accepted on create and carried on `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto`.\n   - Added a read-only `salutation` property to the `Owner` schema.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`**:\n   - Added a persisted `title` column with getter/setter.\n   - Added a derived `getSalutation()` returning `title + ' ' + lastName`, or just `lastName` when the title is null/blank.\n\n3. **Schema files** (`db/hsqldb`, `db/h2`, `db/mysql`, `db/postgres`): added a `title` column to the `owners` table.\n\nThe MapStruct `OwnerMapper` needed no explicit edits \u2014 `title` and `salutation` map automatically by matching property names (`salutation` from `owner.getSalutation()`; enum\u2194String for `title`).\n\n## Verification\n- `AcceptanceTest.coreComposesSalutation` passes (`DR` + `who` \u2192 `\"DR who\"`).\n- Full `./mvnw test` suite: **BUILD SUCCESS**, all tests green.",
